{
  "name": "A/B Split Testing - Chat Prompts",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Keep the same prompt variant for the same chat session.\n// This deterministic assignment avoids needing an external database.\nconst input = $input.first().json;\nconst sessionId = String(input.sessionId ?? input.chatSessionId ?? 'default-session');\nlet hash = 0;\nfor (let i = 0; i < sessionId.length; i++) {\n  hash = ((hash << 5) - hash + sessionId.charCodeAt(i)) | 0;\n}\nconst showAlternative = (Math.abs(hash) % 2) === 1;\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...input,\n    sessionId,\n    show_alternative: showAlternative,\n    variant: showAlternative ? 'alternative' : 'baseline',\n    prompt: showAlternative\n      ? 'You are a helpful assistant. Give short answers'\n      : 'You are a helpful assistant. Give clear, structured answers with a brief explanation and actionable steps.'\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "19e77ec8-bfd1-4689-acae-a42488974299",
      "name": "Assign A/B Prompt Variant",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        272,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A/B Split Testing \nThe Chat Trigger receives a message. The Code node assigns a prompt variant deterministically from the chat session ID, so a session keeps the same variant across messages. The AI Agent uses that prompt.**Before testing:** select your own OpenAI credentials in the OpenAI Chat Model node.\n**Note:** this simplified version does not store analytics or session assignments in Supabase.",
